  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1229 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nSaturday Night and Sunday...An upper-lvl high over the Southwest \n& Texas continues to expand towards the Southeast. As the high \nprogresses, heat indices are expected start increasing to 100 \ndegrees by Sunday. A cut-off low pressure near Gulf states will \ntrack westwards, shifting rain chances through the Interstate 59 \ncorridor and HWY 84 Sunday. \n\nMonday through Friday Night...The aforementioned high will \nsettle over the Southeast CONUS around Tuesday, lingering through \nthe rest of the week. Dangerous heat concerns are expected to \nreturn as highs range in the mid/upper 90s and heat indices reach \n105-110F. HWO graphics may be needed over the next day or two. As \nthe high settles, additional cut-off low disturbances will \ntraverse around the ridge, bring deep moisture and storm chances \n(25-50%) starting along the HWY 84 corridor. Mid-week, rain \nchances will expand to the I-20 corridor and eastern MS as the \npattern lingerns into the end of the week. /SW/",
